      "note": "<p>Fresh Codex reconciliation of preserved independent Tibetan-first and English-first historical proposals. All wording is quoted from the current spine. The fourth alternative is aligned at phrase depth: <code>gnyis ka ma nges pa</code> corresponds to \"definite in neither respect\" as a complete negative quantifier construction. Neither <code>gnyis ka</code> nor <code>ma</code> alone is assigned \"neither\", and neither is falsely marked absent.</p><p>The second alternative's <code>rnam smin</code> is pinned to \"ripen\" in \"not definite to ripen at all\"; the earlier \"should ripen\" is GMR's expansion of the definite occasion. The two adversative <code>la</code> particles license the two \"but\"s; <code>zhes</code> licenses the complementizer \"that\". <code>sde pa</code> owns \"group\"; \"school\" is GMR's accompanying taxonomy word. Number labels, repeated \"deeds\", \"respects\", and the resumptive \"They say there are\" have no separate Tibetan content word. Residual Tibetan consists only of the genitive <code>'i</code>, final <code>'o</code>, and punctuation. C16:756 repeats both columns exactly and is a same-source re-ingest, not independent testimony.</p>"
    },
