      "note": "<p>Fresh Codex reconciliation of the recovered historical proposals. The experienced-in-this-life description <code>mthong chos la myong 'gyur gyi las</code> is retained at d=3 as GMR's complete \"deeds with results that you see in this very life\". This avoids both invented dictionary equivalents and the old proposals' unsupported nulls for <code>myong 'gyur</code>. The repeated predicate <code>ris mthun mi 'phen</code> is represented elliptically by \"do not\"; its complete phrase correspondence is kept at d=3, without dictionary claims that <code>ris mthun</code> means \"do\".</p><p><code>'phen / par / byed</code> are separately \"project / to / act\", not an arbitrary d=5 verb phrase. <code>gnyis pa</code> corresponds to \"Next\", an ordinal use also present in the current HGM glossary; the remaining outline explanation is supplied. <code>zhe na</code> is the campaign's fixed question hinge, tightened to \"may ask\" so the supplied \"One\" is excluded. The current HGM glossary explicitly records <code>'phan</code> as \"projects\" (HTG2016); the source spelling is retained and the historical proposed correction to <code>'phen</code> is not asserted as an erratum. Residual Tibetan after the spans is only genitives and punctuation.</p><p>The trailing \"55 Deeds Projected for Different Realms and Beings\" is a registered following-heading splice. C16:757 has identical Tibetan and identical prose but ends with a different heading, \"19 Deeds that Definitely Ripen\". It is a same-source re-ingest, not an independent witness. No heading or glossary text has been changed.</p>"
