      "note": "<p>Fresh Codex reconciliation of two preserved independent historical proposals. These are six verse lines; their mid-sentence capitals are lineation. GMR's \"does none\" corresponds to the negative predicate <code>mi byed</code> at d=3. The next line's \"Neither\" elliptically reprises <code>myong mi byed</code>; this is a phrase-level correspondence, not a dictionary equivalent for <code>myong</code>, and the content is not falsely labelled unrendered. The final <code>yang min</code> likewise corresponds to \"Neither\" at d=3. <code>gang las</code> and <code>gzhan du'ang</code> remain relative/locative phrases, not invented dictionary units.</p><p>The inflected word <code>dge ba'i</code> carries \"of virtuous\", with its genitive <code>'i</code> explicitly owning \"of\". The inflected demonstrative <code>der</code> carries \"At that\", its bound <code>r</code> licensing \"At\" and <code>de</code> licensing \"that\". The established compound <code>mi brtan pa</code> owns \"unstable\", with the approved negative-affix <code>mi</code> to \"un\" and positive stem <code>brtan pa</code> to \"stable\" as members. The articles, \"has\", \"each\", \"to\", \"he's\", and the conjunction in \"desire and peak\" are supplied; residual Tibetan is two genitive suffixes plus punctuation.</p><p>The verb is quoted as <code>myod</code> exactly as ACIP MYOD. The adjacent parallel predicate has <code>myong mi byed</code>, and C05:173 explains this same line using <code>myong 'gyur</code> and \"experience\". A probable spelling erratum is proposed for separate skeptical review; no correction has been made to either column. The historical claim that <code>myod</code> occurs only here is false: TCS10:338 has <code>myod yul</code> beside <code>myong yul</code>. That is a different passage, not an independent witness to this verse.</p>"
